<!-- ==================== PLATE III — THE IMPLEMENTS ======================= -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">The Craft</p>
    <h2>The Implements, and What They Are Really For</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">Four tools, four cognitive functions. The objects are mnemonics with handles.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid two">
    <figure id="fig-3" class="plate reveal">
      <div class="plate-art plate-art--tall">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 300 300" role="img" aria-label="The wand, a straight rod with a bound grip">
          <g fill="none" stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="1.6">
            <path d="M150 30 L150 270"/>
            <path d="M150 30 q-10 14 0 28 q10 -14 0 -28" stroke="#cf7f8d"/>
            <path d="M140 210 h20 M138 222 h24 M140 234 h20" stroke="#cf7f8d"/>
            <circle cx="150" cy="268" r="6"/>
            <path d="M150 60 q-22 20 -18 56 M150 60 q22 20 18 56" opacity="0.4"/>
          </g>
          <text x="150" y="294" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Cinzel, serif" font-size="12"
                fill="#cf7f8d" letter-spacing="3">WAND · WILL</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <p class="plate-note"><strong>The wand</strong> directs. Traditionally cut to the length of the
      forearm, from a living tree asked first, and never used for anything else. Its function is singular:
      it is the object you pick up when you have decided. ◆ What it actually does is make an intention
      physical and exclusive, and exclusivity is most of the trick — a thing used for one purpose becomes a
      reliable cue for that purpose.</p>
    </figure>

    <figure id="fig-4" class="plate reveal">
      <div class="plate-art plate-art--tall">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 300 300" role="img" aria-label="The cup, a chalice on a stem">
          <g fill="none" stroke="#7fb6d9" stroke-width="1.6">
            <path d="M104 86 q46 78 46 78 q0 0 46 -78 Z"/>
            <path d="M104 86 H196"/>
            <path d="M150 164 V222"/>
            <path d="M112 248 q38 -26 76 0 q-38 14 -76 0 Z"/>
            <path d="M118 102 q32 16 64 0" opacity="0.6"/>
          </g>
          <path d="M106 90 q44 60 44 60 q0 0 44 -60 Z" fill="#7fb6d9" fill-opacity="0.12" stroke="none"/>
          <text x="150" y="294" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Cinzel, serif" font-size="12"
                fill="#7fb6d9" letter-spacing="3">CUP · FEELING</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <p class="plate-note"><strong>The cup</strong> receives. It holds what is offered and what is shared,
      and it is the only implement that passes from hand to hand — which is the point. ◆ The communal drink
      is among the most widespread human ritual acts on record, and its function is social bonding through
      synchronised, witnessed consumption. A rite with nothing shared is a performance with an audience.</p>
    </figure>

    <figure id="fig-5" class="plate reveal">
      <div class="plate-art plate-art--tall">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 300 300" role="img" aria-label="The blade, a double-edged knife point downward">
          <g fill="none" stroke="#9b7ddb" stroke-width="1.6">
            <path d="M150 268 L132 150 L150 44 L168 150 Z"/>
            <path d="M150 44 V268" opacity="0.5"/>
            <path d="M112 150 H188"/>
