      </div>
      <p class="plate-note"><strong>The pentacle</strong> grounds. A flat disc that things are placed
      <em>upon</em> — the written intention, the object to be consecrated, the bread. ◆ Scholarship: the
      five-pointed star is a Pythagorean figure, a Christian symbol of the five wounds, a Mesopotamian sign,
      and only became shorthand for the occult in the nineteenth century via Éliphas Lévi. Point up is the
      ordinary orientation. The inversion's modern meaning is about 170 years old.</p>
    </figure>
